{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-g2-reviewer-fable-34","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:34c19f723e535aa477ad","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"data/input.csv contains exactly 28 data rows with 28 distinct colony_id values (BT-01 through BT-28) and 28 distinct arena_id values; no independent unit appears in more than one row.","observed_value":{"data_rows":28,"distinct_colony_ids":28,"distinct_arena_ids":28,"max_rows_per_colony":1},"source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":1,"quoted_text":"colony_id,arena_id,treatment,founding_workers,gyne_count"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"BT-01,ARENA-01,control,42,14"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":29,"end_line":29,"quoted_text":"BT-28,ARENA-28,exposed,39,5"}]},{"description":"The data description names colony_id as the independent-unit column and states that each colony contributes exactly one row with a single lifetime outcome, so a row-independent two-sample test applies to the rows as given.","observed_value":null,"source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":11,"end_line":11,"quoted_text":"Independent unit column: colony_id"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":15,"end_line":15,"quoted_text":"- colony_id: colony label, unique across the file; no colony is entered twice."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":23,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"Because each colony is measured once and contributes exactly one row, the twenty-eight\nrows are twenty-eight independent units, and a row-independent two-sample test applies\ndirectly, with no pooling of within-colony repeats."}]},{"description":"The analysis code builds one gyne_count value per row per treatment arm with a simple filter comprehension and passes those lists directly to Welch's t-test; there is no join, expansion, resampling, or replication step that could enter a colony more than once.","observed_value":{"control_n":14,"exposed_n":14},"source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":48,"end_line":51,"quoted_text":"    gynes = {\n        arm: [int(r[\"gyne_count\"]) for r in rows if r[\"treatment\"] == arm]\n        for arm in ARMS\n    }"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":60,"end_line":60,"quoted_text":"    tt = stats.ttest_ind(gynes[\"control\"], gynes[\"exposed\"], equal_var=False)"}]},{"description":"The report's own independence check and group tables match the raw data: 28 rows, 28 colonies, at most 1 row per colony, and 14 colonies per arm; the reported means (13.86 and 6.00) reproduce from the raw per-colony gyne counts (sums 194/14 and 84/14), confirming each colony was counted exactly once in the selected Welch t-test result.","observed_value":{"control_mean":13.857142857142858,"exposed_mean":6,"reported_t":4.65,"reported_df":24.5},"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":12,"end_line":13,"quoted_text":"Independence check: 28 data rows, 28 distinct colony identifiers, 28 distinct arena\nidentifiers, at most 1 row per colony."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":26,"end_line":27,"quoted_text":"| control | 14 | 13.86 | 4.99 |\n| exposed | 14 | 6.00 | 3.88 |"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":35,"end_line":35,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Welch's two-sided two-sample t-test on lifetime gyne count with one colony per row: control colonies produced 13.86 gynes on average against 6.00 for thiamethoxam-exposed colonies, a difference of 7.86 gynes (t = 4.65, df = 24.5, p < 0.001), so 2 ppb dietary thiamethoxam is associated with markedly reduced gyne output."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The only candidate structure that could hide a repeated-unit or shared-unit dependence is arena_id, and the analysis independence claims ultimately rest on the description's statement of a single teardown census. However, each arena held exactly one colony (28 distinct arenas for 28 rows), and nothing in the supplied files contradicts the single-census claim, so this does not amount to evidence of repeated independent-unit entry.","observed_value":{"distinct_arena_ids":28,"rows":28},"source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":16,"end_line":16,"quoted_text":"- arena_id: the sealed flight arena the colony occupied; one arena held one colony."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":12,"end_line":13,"quoted_text":"Independence check: 28 data rows, 28 distinct colony identifiers, 28 distinct arena\nidentifiers, at most 1 row per colony."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I tried to demonstrate the issue by searching for any path through which a colony could enter the two-sample tests more than once: I scanned all 28 CSV data rows for duplicate colony_id or arena_id values (none; BT-01..BT-28 and ARENA-01..ARENA-28 each appear exactly once), checked that per-arm sample sizes (14 + 14) sum to the number of distinct colonies rather than exceeding it, recomputed the arm means from raw counts (control 194/14 = 13.86, exposed 84/14 = 6.00) and the Welch t-statistic (7.86 / sqrt(4.99^2/14 + 3.88^2/14) ≈ 4.65), which match the report and are only consistent with one observation per colony, and inspected analysis.py for any join, concatenation, resampling, or row-expansion step (there is none; rows are read once and filtered by treatment). Every check failed to produce the issue.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]}